      "text": "32 ft = 8 * x ft\nx = 32 ft / 8 ft\nBecause the area = (x * x) square ft,\nArea = (32 ft/8 ft * 1 ft) square ft\nArea = 4 ft * 1 ft\nArea = 4 square ft\n\n$\\boxed{4}$\n\nTo solve this problem, we need to find the area of a square with a given perimeter. We are provided with the perimeter of the square as 32 feet.\n\n1. First, we need to determine the length of one side of the square. Since the perimeter of a square is given by 32 ft, and knowing that a square has four equal sides, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter} = 4 \\times \\text{side length}\n\\]\n\nGiven that the perimeter is 32 feet:\n\n\\[\n32 \\text{ ft} = 4 \\times x \\text{ ft}\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), which is the length of one side of the square, we solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{32 \\text{ ft}}{4 \\text{ ft}} = 8 \\text{ ft}\n\\]\n\n2. Now we know each side of the square is 8 feet long. To find the area of the square, we use the formula for the area of a square:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\text{side length}^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the side length we found:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = (8 \\text{ ft})^2 = 64 \\text{ square ft}\n\\]\n\nHence, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{64}\n\\]",
